[Term]
id: DOID:4481
name: allergic rhinitis
alt_id: DOID:12089
alt_id: DOID:14030
alt_id: DOID:8241
alt_id: DOID:8242
def: "A rhinitis that is an allergic inflammation and irritation of the nasal airways involving sneezing, runny nose, nasal congestion, itching and tearing of the eyes caused by exposure to an allergen such as pollen, dust, mold, animal dander and droppings of cockroaches or house dust mites." [url:http\://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Allergic_rhinitis, url:http\://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rhinitis, url:https\://www.merriam-webster.com/dictionary/allergic%20rhinitis#medicalDictionary] {comment="ls:IEDB"}
